.TH VTS 1 2026-11-17 "vts 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vts \- Video Terminal Shell, a terminal client for YouTube
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vts
.RB [ \-c
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-\-offline ]
.br
.B vts
.RI [ option ]...\&
.I command
.RI [ argument ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vts
searches YouTube, shows video pages, comments, channels and playlists,
plays videos with
.BR mpv (1)
and downloads them with
.BR yt\-dlp (1),
all without a Google account.
It keeps a list of favourite channels on your computer and sends a
desktop notification for each of their new videos.
History, Watch later and your own playlists stay on your computer too.
.PP
Without a command,
.B vts
starts the full screen app (see
.BR "THE APP" ).
With a command, it prints what was asked and ends, for scripts and
quick looks.
On a terminal, results take two lines each; otherwise they are one line
of tab\-separated fields, and
.B \-\-json
prints JSON.
.PP
A
.I VIDEO
is an 11\-character identifier or any YouTube link to it (watch, youtu.be,
shorts, live, embed).
A
.I CHANNEL
is its identifier (UC...), its handle (@name) or a link to it.
A
.I PLAYLIST
is its identifier or a link with list=.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " file" "\fR, \fP\-\-config " file
Read the settings from
.I file
instead of
.I ~/.config/vts/config
(on Windows,
.IR %APPDATA%\evts\econfig ).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Say more about what happens.
.TP
.B \-\-offline
No updates of the rules or of yt\-dlp, whatever the settings say.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the help and exit.
Each command has its own:
.BI "vts " command " \-\-help" .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Searching and looking
.TP
.BI "search " "\fR[\fPoption\fR]...\fP words" ...
Search, with the website's filters:
.BI \-t " type"
(video, shorts, channel, playlist, movie),
.BI \-d " when"
(hour, today, week, month, year),
.BI \-l " length"
(short, under 3 minutes; medium, 3 to 20; long, over 20),
.BI \-f " list"
(live, 4k, hd, subtitles, cc, 360, vr180, 3d, hdr, location, purchased,
comma\-separated),
.BI \-s " order"
(relevance, date, views, rating),
.BI \-p " n"
pages of results,
.B \-j
for JSON.
.TP
.BI "suggest " words ...
What the search box suggests, one per line.
.TP
.BI "info " "\fR[\fP\-r n\fR] [\fP\-j\fR]\fP video"
The video page: title, channel, views, date, likes, description,
chapters and
.I n
videos up next (5 by default).
.TP
.BI "comments " "\fR[\fP\-n\fR] [\fP\-r\fR] [\fP\-p n\fR] [\fP\-j\fR]\fP video"
Its comments, top ones first, or newest first with
.BR \-n ;
with
.BR \-r ,
the first replies to each.
.TP
.BI "channel " "\fR[\fP\-t tab\fR] [\fP\-s words\fR] [\fP\-p n\fR] [\fP\-j\fR]\fP channel"
A channel's videos, shorts, live streams or playlists
.RI ( tab ),
or its search results for
.IR words .
.TP
.BI "playlist " "\fR[\fP\-p n\fR] [\fP\-j\fR]\fP playlist"
The videos of a playlist.
.TP
.BI "feed " "\fR[\fP\-n\fR] [\fP\-j\fR]\fP channel"
A channel's latest uploads from its public feed, without Shorts with
.BR \-n .
.SS Watching
.TP
.BI "play " "\fR[\fPoption\fR]...\fP video\fR|\fPplaylist" ...
Play with mpv, one after the other, from where you stopped last time;
where you stop goes into the history.
.BI \-q " quality"
(best, 2160, 1440, 1080, 720, 480, 360, 240, 144),
.B \-a
for the sound only,
.BI \-\-sound\-quality " q"
for the sound only in that quality (high, medium, low),
.BI \-s " speed"
(0.25 to 4),
.BI \-\-subs " langs"
(fr,en),
.B \-t
to draw the video in the terminal,
.BI \-\-from " time"
(1:23) for the first video,
.B \-n
to start from the beginning.
.TP
.BI "subtitles " video
The subtitles the video has: their code, for
.BR "play \-\-subs" ,
and their name.
.TP
.BI "download " "\fR[\fP\-q quality\fR] [\fP\-a\fR] [\fP\-\-audio\-format f\fR] [\fP\-\-sound\-quality q\fR] [\fP\-d dir\fR]\fP video\fR|\fPplaylist" ...
Download with yt\-dlp, into the current folder or
.IR dir :
the video in
.IR quality ,
or the sound only with
.B \-a
(as YouTube has it) or
.BI \-\-audio\-format " f"
(mp3, m4a, opus, flac, wav; ffmpeg makes them), in the quality of
.BI \-\-sound\-quality " q"
(high, medium, low; by default the
.B sound_quality
setting).
.SS Your library
.TP
.B fav
Your favourite channels:
.B "vts fav"
lists them;
.BI "fav add " "\fR[\fP\-g group\fR]\fP channel" ...\&
and
.BI "fav remove " channel ...\&
change the list;
.BI "fav set " "channel " notify=yes|no " " shorts=yes|no " " group= name
sets whether its new videos are notified, whether its Shorts count and
its group;
.BI "fav import " file
adds the channels of Google Takeout's
.I subscriptions.csv
or of an OPML file;
.B "fav export"
prints them as OPML
.RB ( \-\-csv
for Takeout's format).
.TP
.B history
What you watched, most recent first, and where you stopped
.RB ( \-n
.IR n ,
.BR \-\-json );
.BI "history remove " video ...\&
and
.B "history clear"
forget.
.TP
.B later
Watch later;
.BI "later add " video ...\&
and
.BI "later remove " video ...\&
change it.
.TP
.B list
Your playlists:
.BI "list show " name ,
.BI "list create " name ,
.BI "list delete " name ,
.BI "list rename " "name new" ,
.BI "list add " "name video" ...,
.BI "list remove " "name video" ....
.SS Notifications and upkeep
.TP
.BI "check " "\fR[\fP\-q\fR] [\fP\-n\fR] [\fP\-j\fR]\fP"
Look for new videos of your favourite channels, print them and send a
desktop notification for each (none with
.BR \-n ,
nothing printed with
.BR \-q ).
A channel's first check only notes what is there.
.TP
.BI "check \-\-install " "\fR[\fPminutes\fR]\fP"
Check every
.I minutes
(30 by default) with a systemd user timer (on Windows, a scheduled task);
.B "check \-\-uninstall"
removes it.
Where the desktop allows it, each notification has buttons:
.B Play
and
.BR "Watch later" .
.TP
.BR "update " [ \-\-rules | \-\-yt\-dlp ]
Update now what vts updates on its own (see
.BR UPDATES ).
.TP
.B doctor
Try everything (settings, library, mpv, yt\-dlp and its age, deno,
ffmpeg, the notifier, the timer, the rules, a search, a video page, a
feed, suggestions, thumbnails) and say what to fix.
Exits with 1 when something doesn't work.
.TP
.B config
Show the settings in use and where they come from;
.B "config \-\-help"
says what each one does, its values and its default;
.B "config \-\-init"
writes a settings file with all of them explained;
.BI "config set " "key value"
changes one in the settings file.
.SH THE APP
.B vts
alone opens the app: Home (videos you were watching, and the new videos
of your favourites), Search, Favourites, Library (Watch later, your
playlists, the downloads, the history) and Settings, a page for each
video, channel and playlist, and comments.
What you watched is marked in the lists (watched, or where you stopped).
mpv plays in its own window while you keep browsing; the top bar shows
where it is.
In a terminal 100 columns wide or more, the selected result is shown on
the right, with its thumbnail.
.PP
The main keys
.RB ( ? " shows them all):"
.TP 14
.B b
The next site (YouTube, Twitch, SOOP), each with its screens and
colours.
.TP
.BR 1 " " 2 " " 3 " " 4
Home, Favourites, Library, Settings (each one explained, changed in
place, the checks of
.B "vts doctor"
and the updates of
.BR "vts update" ).
On Favourites:
.B N
adds a channel,
.B i
imports,
.B e
exports.
.TP
.BR / ", " s
Search; your recent searches come first, then suggestions as you type;
Tab or the arrows pick one, Delete forgets a recent one, Esc (or
Backspace with nothing typed) cancels;
.B F
sets the filters of the results. A link (of a video, a channel or a
playlist) or a channel's @handle opens what it names.
.TP
.BR Enter ", " Backspace
Open, go back
.RB ( h ,
Esc too).
.TP
.BR j " " k ", arrows"
Move;
.BR g " " G ,
PgUp, PgDn too.
.TP
.BR p " " P " " a
Play, play from here on, the sound only.
.TP
.B Q
Play in a quality chosen from a menu; for the sound only, a second menu
asks high, medium or low.
.TP
.B u
Subtitles, chosen from those the video has; while a video plays, its
subtitles change and it goes on.
.TP
.B d
Download: the video in a quality, or the sound only (as YouTube has it,
MP3, M4A, Opus, FLAC), chosen from a menu; for the sound, then high,
medium or low.
.TP
.BR w " " + " " A
Watch later, add to a playlist, add to what plays.
.TP
.BR c " " f " " y
Go to the channel, make it a favourite, copy the link.
.TP
.BR C " " t " " D
On a video page: comments, chapters, the whole description.
.TP
.BR Space " " < " " > " " x
While playing: pause, previous, next, stop.
.TP
.BR , " " . " " 9 " " 0 " " m
While playing: back and forward 10 seconds, volume down and up, mute.
.TP
.B T
While playing: go to one of its chapters.
.TP
.B V
While playing: go on in another quality, from where it is.
.TP
.BR \- ", Delete"
Remove from a playlist, the history or the favourites; in Downloads,
stop one or take it off the list (Enter plays the file).
.TP
.B r
Load again (on Home: look for new videos).
.TP
.B q
Back, and quit from a section.
.PP
The mouse works: click to select, double\-click to open, the wheel to
scroll.
.SH SETTINGS
.I ~/.config/vts/config
(on Windows,
.IR %APPDATA%\evts\econfig )
holds lines of
.IB key " = " value ;
.B #
starts a comment.
.B "vts config \-\-help"
explains them, and the app's Settings
.RB ( 4 )
change them.
.TP
.BI language " = code"
Language of YouTube's results (fr, en\-GB, pt\-BR); from
.B LANG
by default.
.TP
.BI region " = CC"
Country of the results (FR); empty for YouTube's guess.
.TP
.BI quality " = height"
best, audio, 2160, 1440, 1080 (the default), 720, 480, 360, 240 or 144.
.TP
.BI sound_quality " = q"
The sound only, played or downloaded: high (the default, the best
YouTube has), medium (about 128 kbit/s) or low (about 64 kbit/s).
.TP
.BI subtitles " = langs"
Subtitle languages for mpv (fr,en); empty for none.
.TP
.BI player " = program"
What plays (mpv).
.TP
.BI downloader " = program"
What downloads (yt\-dlp); mpv uses it too, to play.
.TP
.BI notifier " = program"
What notifies (notify\-send); on Windows, its own notifications are used.
.TP
.BI downloads " = folder"
Where downloads go: from the app, and from
.B "vts download"
without
.BR \-d ;
.B ~/
is your home.
Your Downloads folder by default (in the app; the current folder for
.BR "vts download" ).
.TP
.BR notifications " = " yes | no
Desktop notifications of new videos.
.TP
.BR thumbnails " = " auto | blocks | sixel | kitty | iterm2 | no
How the app shows thumbnails: as the terminal's name says (auto, the
default), in coloured blocks, or in one of the image formats.
.TP
.BR updates " = " yes | no
Automatic updates of the rules and of yt\-dlp.
.TP
.BR start_site " = " youtube | twitch | soop | last
The site vts opens on; last: the one it was on when it quit.
.TP
.BR twitch.quality " = " best | 1080 | 720 | 480 | 360 | 160 | audio
The quality of Twitch's live streams.
.TP
.BR soop.quality ", " soop.vod_quality " = " best | 1080 | 720 | 540 | 360 | audio
The quality of SOOP's live streams, and of its past broadcasts.
.SH UPDATES
YouTube changes its pages often.
Where things are in its answers is described by rules, data built into
vts.
Once a day the app and
.B "vts check"
fetch newer rules from vts' repository and keep them in
.I ~/.cache/vts/rules.json
if they are complete, newer and load without error; otherwise the
built\-in rules stay in use.
Once a week, yt\-dlp is told to update itself when you can replace it
(installed by you, not by the system's packages).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/vts/config
The settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/vts/vts.db
The library: favourites, seen videos, history, playlists, recent
searches, downloads (SQLite).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/vts/
The web client version, updated rules, thumbnails, the app's log
.RI ( vts.log )
and mpv's
.RI ( mpv.log ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/vts\-check.timer
The timer of
.BR "vts check \-\-install" .
.PP
On Windows: the settings in
.IR %APPDATA%\evts ,
the library in
.IR %LOCALAPPDATA%\evts ,
the cache in
.IR %LOCALAPPDATA%\evts\ecache .
.PP
The XDG variables
.RB ( XDG_CONFIG_HOME ,
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ,
.BR XDG_CACHE_HOME ,
.BR XDG_RUNTIME_DIR )
are honoured.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when something failed, 2 for a bad command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
vts search \-t video \-d week \-s views linux kernel
vts info https://youtu.be/dQw4w9WgXcQ
vts channel \-t shorts @kurzgesagt
vts fav import subscriptions.csv
vts check \-\-install
vts play \-a \-s 1.5 PLFs4vir_WsTxontcYm5ctqp89cNBJKNrs
.fi
.SH PRIVACY
vts has no account and sends no telemetry.
It talks only to YouTube's own sites (and to vts' repository for the
rules); the only cookie it sends is YouTube's consent answer.
Everything you keep stays in your files.
.PP
Some things need a Google account and are out of reach: liking,
commenting, subscribing on YouTube's side, YouTube's recommendations,
age\-restricted and members\-only videos.
